      "existing_authored_summary_fields": {
        "version_verified": "2021 original research; Water Science & Technology 83(5):1055–1071; DOI 10.2166/wst.2021.039",
        "observed_subject_operation_units_types": "The study uses variable wastewater from one German manufacturer, with submicron through coarse particle sizes. MF is rated in nm; UF/NF use Da cutoffs. Cross-flow, feed history, membrane age, fouling, pressure and chemical cleaning affect results. MF ran at 1 bar; other pilot membranes at 20 bar; pilot maximum is 25 bar. A seven-day MF test displays its first 100 hours.",
        "conditions_defaults_domain_exceptions": "Industrial membrane trials are an analogy, not cartridge proof. The candidate does not equate Da with a particle aperture or adopt these settings. Small-workshop membrane selection and dissolved-ion treatment remain separate investigated questions."
      }
